# IN THE GARDEN - Johnny Cash/John Prine & Mac Wiseman
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
{ns}
{define: C/G base-fret 1 frets 3 3 2 0 1 0} 
{define: E7 base-fret 1 frets 0 2 0 1 0 0} 
{define: F base-fret 1 frets x x 3 2 1 1} 
{define: Fm base-fret 1 frets x x 3 1 1 1} 
{define: F/C base-fret 1 frets x 3 3 2 1 1} 
{t: IN THE GARDEN - Johnny Cash/John Prine & Mac Wiseman }
{st: (Miles) }
{artist: Johnny Cash; John Prine; Mac Wiseman }
{composer: Miles }


https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u29eXL75Zfk   (Prine/Wiseman)  (Capo 2)

https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=py-_VnHv3gg  (Cash)  (Capo 0)

This old gospel hymn dates back to 1912 and has been recorded by many over the years.  I prefer the starker beauty of these two versions, one by Johnny Cash and the other by John Prine and Mac Wiseman.  Note Johnny includes one extra verse that the others do not.  Marked accordingly.

TIP:  For the intro (if untransposed) form (C/G) which is just (C) with your pinky covering the bass (g) on the top string/3rd fret.  Then pick the covered 5th string (c) and strum, then the covered 6th string (g) and strum, repeat.

TIP:  The chorus has an (F) to (Fm) transition which isn't too bad.  Instead of playing a regular (F) play an (F/C) which is just (F) with your pinky covering the bass (c) 5th string/3rd fret.  Then from the (F/C) keep your ring and pinky where they are and lift your middle finger while moving your index finger up one additional string to cover the 3rd string/1st fret.   

TIP:  In the little instrumental bridge for the Prine/Wiseman version you repeat the chords from the verse.


